B.fHx=new A.e6("oil","Oil price (WTI crude)","The price of West Texas Intermediate crude oil, in dollars per barrel: the US benchmark for the world's most important energy input.","Energy is getting costlier: inflation pressure rises and consumers have less to spend elsewhere. Can also signal strong demand.","Energy is cheaper: easing inflation pressure and lower costs for airlines and consumers. Can also signal weak demand.","Oil rising \u2014 inflation pressure up.","Oil falling \u2014 inflation pressure down.","At {v}, the oil price is within its ordinary range.","At {v}, oil is unusually high or low against its history.","At {v}, oil is at an extreme of its history.",B.cZw,B.dep,"Energy producers gain; airlines, cruise lines and transport lose.",B.d8q,B.axY)
