B.fHr=new A.e6("gold","Gold price","The price of gold futures in dollars per ounce. Gold pays no interest, so it competes with bonds and tends to rise when real yields fall or when investors want a store of value.","Falling real yields, a weaker dollar, inflation worries, or a rush to safety \u2014 or central-bank buying.","Rising real yields or a strong dollar make bonds more attractive than gold.","Gold rising \u2014 safety demand or falling real yields.","Gold falling \u2014 higher real yields or a stronger dollar.","At {v}, gold is within its ordinary range.","At {v}, gold is unusually high or low against its history.","At {v}, gold is at an extreme of its history.",B.cQL,B.ddo,"Gold miners (which can move more than gold itself).",B.d8h,B.aAT)
