B.cMU=s(["Prices rise faster than wages \u2192 households cut back.","The Fed raises rates to cool demand \u2192 borrowing costs rise.","Higher rates lower stock and bond prices, and slow hiring."],t.s)
B.hoU=new A.L("Jun 2022","US CPI inflation peaked near 9.1%, the highest since 1981.")
B.hm1=new A.L("Mar 1980","Inflation peaked near 14.8% before the Volcker Fed's rate hikes broke it.")
B.hlw=new A.L("May 2020 (approx.)","Inflation fell near 0% as the pandemic shut the economy.")
B.d04=s([B.hoU,B.hm1,B.hlw],t.L)
B.axX=s(["corepce","breakeven","oil"],t.s)
B.fH1=new A.e6("cpi","CPI inflation (year over year)","The yearly change in the Consumer Price Index: how much more a typical household basket costs than a year ago. Shown here as a % change from the monthly index.","Prices are rising faster. The Fed is more likely to hold or raise rates, and real incomes are squeezed.","Disinflation: price pressure is easing, opening room for rate cuts.","Inflation heating up \u2014 rate-cut hopes fade.","Inflation cooling \u2014 more room for cuts.","At {v}, headline inflation is near the range the Fed is comfortable with.","At {v}, inflation is well above the Fed's 2% goal.","At {v}, inflation is high enough to force aggressive tightening.",B.cOZ,B.cMU,"Energy and commodity producers benefit from inflation; consumer discretionary and long-duration growth are squeezed.",B.d04,B.axX)
B.hpO=new A.L("Below 2.5%","Near the 2% target (calm).")
B.huN=new A.L("2.5% to 4%","Above target (watch).")
B.hl8=new A.L("4% or more","Well above target (stress).")
B.d39=s([B.hpO,B.huN,B.hl8],t.L)
B.cYJ=s(["Core strips out volatile food and energy to show the trend.","The Fed sets its 2% target on total PCE; core is its guide to where it is heading.","Persistent core readings above target keep policy tight."],t.s)
B.hlU=new A.L("Early 2022 (approx.)","Core PCE inflation rose above 5%, the highest in about four decades.")
B.d2b=s([B.hlU],t.L)
B.axZ=s(["cpi","breakeven","unrate"],t.s)
B.fGh=new A.e6("corepce","Core PCE inflation (year over year)","The yearly change in the Personal Consumption Expenditures price index excluding food and energy \u2014 the inflation gauge the Federal Reserve targets.","Underlying inflation is firmer. This is the number the Fed watches most for rate decisions.","Underlying inflation is cooling toward the 2% target.","Underlying inflation firming.","Underlying inflation cooling toward target.","At {v}, core inflation is close to the Fed's 2% goal.","At {v}, core inflation is above the Fed's goal.","At {v}, core inflation is far above the Fed's goal.",B.d39,B.cYJ,"Same as CPI: tight policy hurts rate-sensitive sectors.",B.d2b,B.axZ)
B.hjY=new A.L("1.8% to 2.6%","Anchored near target (calm).")
B.hpp=new A.L("Outside that band","Drifting (watch).")
B.hnq=new A.L("Below 1.0% or above 3.2%","Extreme (stress).")
B.d_V=s([B.hjY,B.hpp,B.hnq],t.L)
B.daV=s(["Breakeven = nominal yield \u2212 real yield.","A jump with oil prices shows the market extrapolating energy costs.","Falling breakevens in a selloff can mean deflation fear, not good news."],t.s)
B.huq=new A.L("Late 2008 and Mar 2020","The 10-year breakeven fell below 1% in both crises as deflation fear took over.")
