B.fGI=new A.e6("tga","Treasury General Account (TGA)","The US Treasury's checking account at the Fed. When the Treasury spends, money flows out into the banking system; when it collects taxes or sells bonds and builds cash, money flows in and reserves drain.","The Treasury is hoarding cash: reserves are being drained from the banking system.","The Treasury is spending its cash down: reserves are being added.","Treasury cash building \u2014 liquidity draining.","Treasury cash falling \u2014 liquidity added.","At {v}, the TGA is within its usual range.","At {v}, the TGA is unusually high or low against its history.","At {v}, the TGA is at an extreme of its history.",B.dgw,B.cK_,"Money markets, banks and speculative assets are most sensitive.",B.cgR,B.aAk)
