B.eHd=new A.b(B.h,["Ranks symbols (or segments) by how unusual their recent behaviour is compared with what their sector, the market and the macro backdrop explain. It is a list of things worth a look, not of things to buy."],t.w)
B.eT9=new A.b(B.h,["Six rules, each scaled 0 to 3, then a weighted mean of the ones that can be read (at least two needed). (1) Unexplained move: the 4- or 13-week return minus beta times its benchmark's return (sector ETF for a sector member, else SPY), divided by the spread of its own earlier misses; 3 or more = 3. (2) Volume: this week over the 26-week median before it; 5 times = 3. (3) Volatility: the last 4 weeks' swing over the 52 weeks before; 3 times = 3. (4) Breakout: relative strength vs SPY at a new 26-week high while its sector's 13-week relative strength is negative. (5) Macro habit: its 13-week return minus beta times the move of bonds, the dollar or oil (beta from the 104 weeks ending 13 weeks ago), as a multiple of its usual miss; the driver with the biggest miss is named. (6) Filings activity over its 26-week median, only with Portfolios. A segment scores the median of its ranked members."],t.w)
B.eBx=new A.b(B.h,["Unusual is not the same as good: a big surprise can be bad news. Betas and spreads are estimated from past data and can shift. Skipped rules are listed on each row, never filled with made-up values. Needs volume data from your forge for the volume rule."],t.w)
