B.Rx=new A.C("confirmDelete",B.ab,"Ask to confirm before a swipe/menu delete removes a row (default off).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h1v=new A.C("builtinDelete",B.ab,"Set false to suppress the engine's own row Delete everywhere it would otherwise appear (long-press row menu AND the default \"delete\" swipe entry) \u2014 default true, exact prior behavior when omitted. Use when the applet declares its OWN guarded delete (e.g. confirms an item count, refuses when shared) so a more-discoverable built-in Delete can't bypass it and orphan data.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fYQ=new A.C("bubbles",B.a_,'Opt-in chat-bubble row styling: { byColumn, selfValue, example }. Rows whose byColumn value matches the resolved selfValue (a literal, or a token like $playerId / $rowId / $selected:<table>) render end-aligned + tinted ("me"); everything else (including an unset selfValue token) renders start-aligned + neutral ("them"). Absent entirely -> the plain ListTile row, unchanged. Optional `example: { ids: [...], label, hideLabel, chipLabel, hiddenFromSetting, onHide }` marks demo-content rows (house-design-rules.md rule 10): each listed row id gets a small "example" chip (chipLabel, localizable), a slim label+divider (label, localizable) renders once above the first such row with a Hide action (hideLabel + onHide, an action spec), and when the named `hiddenFromSetting` board setting resolves truthy (\'1\'/\'true\') those rows are dropped from the list entirely. Optional `attachmentsColumn` (chatnest-1029): a column holding inline attachment maps ({name, mime, data}) shown inside the bubble \u2014 image thumbnails and file chips above the text; an attachment-only row shows no empty text line. Absent -> unchanged. Optional markdown (bubbles-markdown-1029): `markdown: true` renders every bubble\'s title text as markdown (bold/italic/lists/code/links; raw HTML shown inert, images never fetched \u2014 alt-text placeholder, links via the checked-link path, code blocks scroll). `markdownColumn: <col>` instead decides PER ROW: markdown only when that column is truthy (true/1/"true"/"1"; falsy/absent = literal text) and takes precedence over `markdown`. `markdownSetting: <key>` decides for EVERY row from that board setting (unset = on; false/off = literal text), old rows included, and takes precedence over both. `markdownRoles: [..]` limits markdown to rows whose `byColumn` value is in the list (e.g. ["assistant"]). Subtitle/meta stay plain. All absent -> literal text, unchanged. Optional copy (chatx-1031): `selectable: true` makes the bubble text drag-selectable (not installed on touch when copyAction is on, where long-press is the Copy gesture); `copyAction: true` adds a per-message Copy: a hover icon beside the bubble on mouse, and a Copy entry in the long-press / right-click menu. Copies the RAW stored text (markdown source) and toasts "Copied". Both absent -> unchanged. Optional `rowActions` (row-actions-1031): per-message actions, same entry shape and gestures as the list-level `rowActions` prop (takes precedence over it for bubble rows); on mouse they show as a compact icon strip under the hovered/focused bubble. Optional `chat` (chatcap-ui-1031): an AI-chat status layer { statusColumn, noteColumn, thinkingColumn, thinkMsColumn, continuedColumn, sourcesColumn, actionColumn, errorRoles[], labels{thinking,thoughtFor,reasoning,continued,stopped,cutOff,sources,save}, actions{<key>:{label,action}}, byline? (true: the done-summary line ends with "<connName> \xb7 <short model>" from connNameColumn / modelColumn; rows without a connection name show nothing; paid replies that store costUsd / chatCostUsd add "About $0.06 for this reply \xb7 $1.40 for this chat so far") } (labels are localizable maps; defaults English). Rows in an active status (waiting/thinking/streaming/searching/creating/retrying/continuing) show a spinner / "Thinking\u2026" and render PLAIN text (no markdown reflow); a finished reply shows a collapsible "Thought for {n}s" (PLAIN text, untrusted), the note line, chips (continued / stopped / cut off), a Sources list (http(s) only, via the checked-link path) and, via `actions`, one button keyed by the row\'s actionColumn on an error row (errorRoles, default ["error"]; tinted as an error bubble) or by its status (e.g. truncated). Attachments on non-self rows become file chips with a Save button (host `export` callback, basename-sanitized). Absent -> unchanged. Optional `statusLine: true` (aistatus-1101) replaces the spinner / "Thought for" block with the live status line (animated dots, phase word, elapsed time, running token count), per-tool activity rows (own timer, tap to open the details) from the `steps` column, and, once finished, one quiet summary line ("Thought for 12s \xb7 1.1k tokens") that opens to the steps and the PLAIN-text reasoning. Reads columns startedAt, liveTokens, outputTokens, ms, steps (names overridable with startedAtColumn / liveTokensColumn / outputTokensColumn / msColumn / stepsColumn). `actions.stop` adds a Stop button on the status line; `stepActions{approve,decline}` add Approve / Decline buttons on a waiting step (args: id, step, decision). Words are engine strings (21 languages). Reduced motion keeps the dots still.',B.k,null,!1)
B.fWx=new A.C("selectableThread",B.ab,'Opt-in (chatsel-1031): wraps the bubble list in ONE SelectionArea so a single click-drag selects across many bubbles and Cmd/Ctrl+C copies them in order. Requires `bubbles`; with it on, bubbles use the outer area (per-bubble `selectable` is not double-wrapped), row taps, copyAction buttons and markdown links keep working. Each message carries an invisible role label so copied text reads "You: ..." / "Assistant: ..." (localized; nothing visible changes). Known limit: in a very long lazily built list a drag covers only the rows that are currently built; with selectableThread on, the list builds `threadCacheExtent` px (default 20000, roughly 100 messages) past the viewport, so select-all/drag/copy cover about that much - messages beyond it in a longer thread are not included. Applies to the boxed list (incl. anchor:"bottom") and the windowed root. Mouse platforms (row-actions-1031): bubble text shows the I-beam cursor and primary clicks go to selection (double-click word, triple-click paragraph, shift-click extend; the click focuses the area so Cmd/Ctrl+A selects the thread text and Cmd/Ctrl+C copies); a configured row tap still fires on a plain single click that leaves no selection; a bubble never swipes under a mouse (touch/stylus still do); right-click while text is selected puts "Copy selection" at the top of the row menu. The same mouse rules apply to per-bubble `bubbles.selectable`. Absent -> unchanged.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h9e=new A.C("threadCacheExtent",B.aM,"Opt-in (row-actions-1031), with selectableThread only: how far past the viewport (logical px) the thread is built so selection and copy reach older messages. Default 20000 when selectableThread is on.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hfJ=new A.C("rowActions",B.a_,'Opt-in per-row actions (row-actions-1031): a list of entries { id?, icon, label, action, column?, equals?, notEquals?, destructive?, hint?, lastOnly? } - hint (listtree-1102, string or {lang: text} map) is a plain-words explanation shown as a smaller muted second line under the label in the right-click / long-press / more menu, and as the hover-strip tooltip; lastOnly:true (chatcomposer-1102) shows the entry only on the LAST visible, non-deleted row passing its column/equals gate (e.g. Regenerate on the last assistant reply) - label is a string or {lang: text} map; action is a normal action spec fired with the ROW (id + table), like cardActions; column + equals/notEquals gates the entry per row (e.g. Edit only where role == "user"). Built-in entries: { builtin: "copy" } copies the row\'s titleColumn text; { builtin: "softDelete", flag?, label?, icon?, beforeAction?, afterAction? } sets the boolean flag column (default "deleted", or the table\'s registered undoSoftDeleteTables flag) to true, hides flagged rows from this list, and shows a "Deleted - Undo" snackbar whose Undo sets it back to false (no confirm dialog). Declaring the entry also registers the table in BoardState.undoSoftDeleteTables so undo/redo never tombstones its rows; declare the flag as a bool column. beforeAction/afterAction are optional action specs fired with the row around the flag write (a nested child whose parent is hidden already shows top-level via parentColumn). Gestures: mouse - hover (or keyboard focus) reveals a \u22ee button on list rows / an icon strip under bubbles, and right-click opens an anchored menu (never a bottom sheet; Esc dismisses; destructive entries last in the error colour). Touch - swipe left reveals the entries as buttons (touch and stylus only, so a mouse drag still selects text and vertical drags still scroll), and long-press opens the same menu at the touch point. Long-press belongs to the menu: like copyAction, per-bubble `selectable` is not installed on touch while rowActions is on (desktop drag-selection and selectableThread are unaffected). Replaces the built-in Open/Edit/Delete row menu and swipeActions for this node; row tap is unchanged. Absent -> unchanged.',B.k,null,!1)
B.haI=new A.C("rowFilter",B.a_,"Opt-in row filter (chatbundle-1108): { column, truthy } keeps only rows whose flag column is truthy (truthy: true) or not truthy (truthy: false) - e.g. an `archived` flag splitting one table into a main list and an Archived list. Absent -> every row, unchanged.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hib=new A.C("parentColumn",B.K,"Opt-in nesting (chatnest-1029): a self-referential column. A row whose parent is another listed row renders indented directly under it (sortColumn/sortDir apply among top-level rows and among siblings); a row whose parent is not listed is top-level. Absent -> the flat list, unchanged.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hik=new A.C("tree",B.a_,'Opt-in nested-tree mode (listtree-1102), needs parentColumn: { unreadColumn?, workingColumn? } (or true). Any depth; a caret button (expanded/collapsed) folds a row\'s children, remembered per device (local prefs keyed applet + list id + row id, never synced; default expanded); children indent 16 px per level (12 px under 600 px width, capped after level 3 with a small "L4"/"L5" label) with a 1 px guide line per ancestor level. A collapsed parent is followed by a summary row "6 nested - 3 unread - 1 working" (nested = all descendants; unread/working = descendants whose column is truthy, zero parts omitted except nested). A row whose unreadColumn is truthy shows a dot (also on a collapsed parent when any descendant is unread); a truthy workingColumn shows a small spinner. Rows whose parent is missing or soft-deleted are roots. The list id is the node `id`, else the table name. Absent -> unchanged.',B.k,null,!1)
B.fXp=new A.C("selectedId",B.T,"Opt-in current-row highlight (chatnest-1029): a row id or a token (e.g. $selected:<table>); the matching row renders as selected (tinted). Unset/unresolved -> no highlight.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hdG=new A.C("hideEmptyDefault",B.ab,'Opt-in (chatlayout-1102): true drops the engine default "Nothing here yet." empty state when no emptyIcon/emptyTitle/emptyText is set, so an empty list renders nothing. Explicit empty-state props still win. Absent -> unchanged.',B.k,null,!1)
B.Gi=new A.C("emptyIcon",B.T,"Icon name shown atop the empty-state panel (when the source has no rows).",B.k,null,!1)
B.Go=new A.C("emptyTitle",B.T,"Headline for the empty state; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.k,null,!0)
B.Gj=new A.C("emptyText",B.T,"Body text for the empty state; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.k,null,!0)
B.G7=new A.C("emptyAction",B.a_,"Action spec { fn, args } (or bare-string fn) fired by the empty-state button \u2014 e.g. add the first row.",B.k,null,!1)
B.Gf=new A.C("emptyActionLabel",B.T,'Label for the empty-state action button (default "Add"); may be a {lang: text} map.',B.k,null,!0)
B.G9=new A.C("emptyActionIcon",B.T,'Icon name for the empty-state action button (default "add").',B.k,null,!1)
B.Ry=new A.C("example",B.a_,'Opt-in demo-content marking: { ids, column, label, chipLabel, hideLabel, hiddenFromSetting, onHide }. Exactly one of `ids` (a list of row ids) or `column` (rows where this column is truthy) selects the marked rows \u2014 both or neither makes the block invalid and it is ignored. Marked rows get a small "chipLabel" chip (default "Example"); a slim "label" divider (default "EXAMPLES") renders once above the first marked row with a "hideLabel" (default "Hide") action. `onHide` is an optional action spec { fn, args } fired through normal dispatch; when absent, tapping Hide writes `board.settings[hiddenFromSetting] = true` directly \u2014 no host code required. When the named `hiddenFromSetting` board setting resolves truthy (\'1\'/\'true\'), marked rows are dropped from the node entirely. All labels may be a {lang: text} map.',B.k,null,!1)
B.djv=s([B.wP,B.h2u,B.aVW,B.aW5,B.aVF,B.aW3,B.a5F,B.hdH,B.h2N,B.hht,B.aW2,B.Rz,B.a5L,B.aVR,B.Rx,B.h1v,B.fYQ,B.fWx,B.h9e,B.hfJ,B.haI,B.hib,B.hik,B.fXp,B.hdG,B.Gi,B.Go,B.Gj,B.G7,B.Gf,B.G9,B.Ry],t.G)
B.fvL=new A.dv("list","A flat list of a table's rows.",B.djv,!1)
B.had=new A.C("parentColumn",B.K,"Column pointing to the parent row.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fVs=new A.C("titleColumn",B.K,"Column shown as each node title.",B.k,null,!1)
B.Rv=new A.C("statusColumn",B.K,"Column holding done/open state.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fXQ=new A.C("orderColumn",B.K,"Column used to order siblings.",B.k,null,!1)
B.Rw=new A.C("doneValue",B.T,"Value of statusColumn meaning done.",B.k,null,!1)
B.a5N=new A.C("onToggle",B.a_,"Checkbox-toggle action spec.",B.k,null,!1)
B.a5E=new A.C("filterable",B.ab,"Show a live filter control.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hhb=new A.C("addChild",B.ab,'Show a trailing "+" on each row that inserts a child row (parent pre-filled).',B.k,null,!1)
B.qQ=new A.C("fillPhone",B.ab,"Fill the full phone viewport and pan/zoom internally (chrome docked, no page scroll). Defaults from the node type; set false to opt out.",B.k,"Fill viewport (phone)",!1)
B.d8c=s(["hold","off"],t.s)
B.h83=new A.C("reorder",B.bU,'Drag-to-group gesture: "hold" (default) long-presses to select, then drags the selection to re-parent; "off" disables drag-to-group entirely (selection + delete still work).',B.d8c,null,!1)
B.d3o=s([B.wP,B.had,B.fVs,B.Rv,B.fXQ,B.Rw,B.Rz,B.a5L,B.a5N,B.a5E,B.hhb,B.qQ,B.Gi,B.Go,B.Gj,B.G7,B.Gf,B.G9,B.h83],t.G)
B.fvt=new A.dv("tree","A hierarchy from a self-referential column.",B.d3o,!1)
B.aW9=new A.C("dateColumns",B.mD,"Date columns (first present wins).",B.k,null,!1)
B.aVK=new A.C("swipeActions",B.a_,'Opt-in swipe-left reveal buttons (off unless set): objects { label, icon, action, role:"danger" } or builtins "edit"/"delete"; label may be a {lang: text} map.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hi6=new A.C("relativeHeaders",B.ab,'Humanize section headers: "Today"/"Tomorrow"/"Yesterday", a weekday + short date for the next 2-6 days, and the raw date string beyond that (default off \u2014 exact prior behavior).',B.k,null,!1)
B.h1J=new A.C("timeColumn",B.K,'A text column holding "HH:MM" (rules.time). When set, rows within each date section sort by it ascending (empty/unparseable rows last, preserving their existing order) and each row shows the parsed time as a leading label.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h9Q=new A.C("hideWhenEmpty",B.ab,"Opt-in (njnest-1111): with no rows (and no search) the agenda shows nothing at all \u2014 no empty state.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h9y=new A.C("filter",B.a_,"Static pre-filter { column, value|in } \u2014 OR a LIST of such maps, ANDed (same shape as `cards`' filter) \u2014 narrows the source rows before grouping, e.g. keeping a shared table's member/comment rows off the agenda, or combining a kind gate with a board scope.",B.k,null,!1)
B.d_F=s([B.wP,B.aW9,B.a5F,B.Rv,B.Rw,B.Rz,B.a5L,B.a5N,B.a5E,B.aVK,B.Rx,B.hi6,B.h1J,B.h9Q,B.h9y,B.Gi,B.Go,B.Gj,B.G7,B.Gf,B.G9],t.G)
B.fvm=new A.dv("agenda","Rows grouped by their first present date.",B.d_F,!1)
B.fZQ=new A.C("titleColumn",B.K,"Column shown on each day cell.",B.k,null,!1)
B.a5I=new A.C("action",B.a_,"Row-tap action spec { fn, args }.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fXI=new A.C("addAction",B.a_,'Day-tap action { fn, args }; the tapped date is merged into the new row\'s values under dateColumn. weekBoxes: fired by tapping a box\'s empty area or its "+ Tap/Click to add" line \u2014 every "$boxDate" in it becomes the box\'s yyyy-MM-dd (weekend box: its first day) and the date is merged into args.values[dateColumn] of the top-level step or of each addRow step of a chain, e.g. chain addRow {values, select: true} then goto the detail screen.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h23=new A.C("dateColumn",B.K,"Column the tapped date fills for addAction (default first dateColumns).",B.k,null,!1)
B.hah=new A.C("weekStart",B.T,"First day of week: monday (default) or sunday.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hfy=new A.C("weekStartTable",B.b1,"Single-row prefs table whose weekStartColumn overrides weekStart live.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fVn=new A.C("weekStartColumn",B.K,"Column in weekStartTable holding monday|sunday (end-user preference).",B.k,null,!1)
B.fZ3=new A.C("scroll",B.ab,"Continuous vertical scroll through months (centered on the current month) instead of the paged prev/next single month.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fWw=new A.C("continuous",B.ab,"Alias for scroll: continuous vertical scroll through months instead of the paged prev/next single month.",B.k,null,!1)
B.dhb=s(["today","firstWithData"],t.s)
B.h4j=new A.C("initialView",B.bU,'Which month opens first. "today" (default) opens the current month; "firstWithData" opens the earliest month containing any row (by dateColumns-resolved date) \u2014 falls back to today when the table has no dated rows.',B.dhb,null,!1)
B.fXg=new A.C("weekBoxes",B.ab,'Opt-in weekly planner: one box per weekday (Mon\u2013Fri) + a Weekend box for the week holding `$day:<settingKey>`; items show time + title (check-off via doneColumn/doneWhen), today\'s box is highlighted. Wide = 2-column grid; narrow = stacked, an empty day is one "Nothing yet" line. Uses table/dateColumn(s)/timeColumn/titleColumn/kindColumn/kindColors/filter/action like dayAgenda.',B.k,null,!1)
B.heT=new A.C("settingKey",B.T,"weekBoxes: the setting (a daybar's key) whose day picks the week; unset/invalid = this week.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fVC=new A.C("mergeWeekend",B.ab,"weekBoxes: default true \u2014 Saturday + Sunday share one Weekend box (items prefixed with their weekday); false = seven boxes.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hes=new A.C("weekendTint",B.ab,"weekBoxes and dayAgenda month: Saturday + Sunday take the weekend tint (lavender, or the app palette's weekend colours).",B.k,null,!1)
B.d2z=s(["classic","accent"],t.s)
B.hhe=new A.C("todayStyle",B.bU,'weekBoxes and dayAgenda month: "accent" = today in the accent border with a peach header/fill (default: the classic highlight).',B.d2z,null,!1)
B.hhH=new A.C("selectable",B.ab,"weekBoxes (needs settingKey): tapping a box's empty space writes its day to settingKey and marks it \"Adding here\" (unless it is today); replaces addAction's add line. The header still fires dayAction.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fVA=new A.C("undatedBox",B.a_,'weekBoxes: true or {label?, hideDone? (default true)} \u2014 one more box, "To do \xb7 no day yet", listing the filtered rows with no date.',B.k,null,!1)
B.fTG=new A.C("gridColumns",B.aM,"weekBoxes: columns from gridMinWidth (default 2); rows share a bounded height (4 = a 4\xd72 week with undatedBox).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h7L=new A.C("gridMinWidth",B.aM,"weekBoxes: width from which gridColumns applies (default 840).",B.k,null,!1)
B.de2=s(["plain","boxed"],t.s)
B.h7M=new A.C("cellStyle",B.bU,'dayAgenda month: "boxed" = every day a bordered card.',B.de2,null,!1)
B.h2P=new A.C("dayAction",B.a_,'weekBoxes: box-header tap action { fn, args } \u2014 every "$boxDate" in it becomes that box\'s yyyy-MM-dd (the weekend box: its first day), e.g. chain setSetting {key, value: "$boxDate"} then goto.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hei=new A.C("openValue",B.T,"weekBoxes: with doneValue, the doneColumn value written when un-checking a text-valued done column (weekBoxes reads doneValue as the doneColumn value meaning done; default boolean true/false).",B.k,null,!1)
B.hiA=new A.C("dayAgenda",B.ab,"Opt-in month + selected-day agenda: tapping a day shows that day's items (time, kind accent, optional check-off) in the same node \u2014 beside the month on wide screens, under a compact dot-density month on phones. Dates come from dateColumns, else dateColumn. Absent: the classic month grid, unchanged.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hd5=new A.C("timeColumn",B.K,'dayAgenda: an "HH:mm" (rules.time) column; rows sort by it within a day (no time = all day, listed first) and show it in app.clock style.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hfU=new A.C("doneColumn",B.K,"dayAgenda: a boolean column; agenda rows show a checkbox that writes it directly (gated by doneWhen).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h5Y=new A.C("doneWhen",B.a_,"dayAgenda: { column, value|in } (filter shape) limiting which rows get the checkbox, e.g. only to-dos. Absent: every row.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hhf=new A.C("carry",B.a_,"Opt-in carry-through (carry-1108): { startColumn?, doneColumn?, doneAtColumn?, skipIf?: [columns], filter?, label? } or true. An undone row with a start date shows on every day from it on; once done, from start to the doneAt day (no doneAt: the start day only). A set skipIf column (e.g. a time, a repeat) or a row outside filter keeps its own day. weekBoxes: the row is in every box of its span with a span line. dayAgenda month: a span bar per week row (open: solid to today, dashed after); the day agenda lists it.",B.k,null,!1)
B.a5H=new A.C("doneAtColumn",B.K,"Optional (carry-1108): the done toggle also writes this column \u2014 now (UTC ISO-8601) when ticked, cleared when unticked. Default: carry.doneAtColumn.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fWi=new A.C("subtasks",B.a_,"Opt-in subtasks (ndnotes-1109): true or { parentColumn? (default parentId), titleColumn?, doneColumn?, orderColumn?, values?: {\u2026written on each new subtask}, promoteValues?: {\u2026written when reparent makes one top-level}, parentFilter? }. A subtask is a row of the same table whose parentColumn names a live row passing parentFilter, or a subtask itself (ndfix-1110: nesting is unlimited; done/total counts direct subtasks).  weekBoxes: subtasks are not listed; a parent shows done/total.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h0M=new A.C("kindColumn",B.K,"dayAgenda: column whose value picks the row's accent via kindColors.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hfl=new A.C("kindColors",B.a_,"dayAgenda: map of kindColumn value \u2192 color (ramp name or #hex) for day dots and agenda accents.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h3G=new A.C("filter",B.a_,"Static pre-filter { column, value|in } \u2014 OR a LIST of such maps, ANDed (same shape as `cards`' filter) \u2014 narrows the source rows before placing them on the grid, e.g. keeping a shared table's member/comment rows off the calendar, or combining a kind gate with a board scope.",B.k,null,!1)
B.bXq=s([B.wP,B.aW9,B.fZQ,B.Rv,B.Rw,B.a5I,B.fXI,B.h23,B.hah,B.hfy,B.fVn,B.fZ3,B.fWw,B.h4j,B.fXg,B.heT,B.fVC,B.hes,B.hhe,B.hhH,B.fVA,B.fTG,B.h7L,B.h7M,B.h2P,B.hei,B.hiA,B.hd5,B.hfU,B.h5Y,B.hhf,B.a5H,B.fWi,B.h0M,B.hfl,B.h3G],t.G)
B.fwy=new A.dv("calendar","A month grid placing rows on dates.",B.bXq,!1)
B.haM=new A.C("groupColumn",B.K,"Group by this column (vs. by date).",B.k,null,!1)
B.aVD=new A.C("groupOrder",B.a_,"Ordering of group sections (List).",B.k,null,!1)
B.fZC=new A.C("dateColumns",B.mD,"Date columns for time buckets.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fTt=new A.C("subtitleColumns",B.mD,"Columns shown as subtitle.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hif=new A.C("action",B.a_,"Alias for `onTap` (row-tap action spec { fn, args }); either name works \u2014 the shared action dispatch reads `action` first.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hag=new A.C("openValue",B.T,'Value of statusColumn meaning NOT done (default "todo") \u2014 the value the built-in checkbox toggle writes back when un-completing a row.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hfP=new A.C("filter",B.a_,"Static pre-filter { column, value|in } \u2014 OR a LIST of such maps, ANDed (same shape as `cards`' filter) \u2014 narrows the source rows before bucketing, e.g. keeping a shared table's member/comment rows off the board, or combining a kind gate with a board scope.",B.k,null,!1)
B.cJA=s([B.wP,B.haM,B.aVD,B.fZC,B.a5F,B.fTt,B.Rv,B.Rw,B.Rz,B.a5N,B.aVK,B.Rx,B.Gi,B.Go,B.Gj,B.G7,B.Gf,B.G9,B.hif,B.hag,B.hfP],t.G)
B.fv8=new A.dv("buckets","Rows grouped into time buckets or by a column.",B.cJA,!1)
B.fUY=new A.C("table",B.b1,"The source table (default entries).",B.k,null,!1)
B.fTV=new A.C("excludeArchived",B.ab,'dufb17a-0924: drop rows hidden by the ARCHIVE lifecycle (rows whose incoming edges are all type "archived", plus their contains-subtrees), read off this node\'s own edgesTable/edgeFrom/edgeTo/edgeType/containsType keys. Scoped views already never reach them; this covers whole-table use. Absent/false = unchanged.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hbp=new A.C("statusColumn",B.K,"Column holding the lane status value (default status).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h4L=new A.C("prioColumn",B.K,"priolanes2-0726: opt-in \u2014 switches to the 4-lane Now/Next/Queued/Later definition keyed by this column's own value instead of statusColumn. A row with no value here falls back to the status mapping (active->Now, queued->Queued, discussed->Later); unset (default) preserves the original 3-lane statusColumn-only behavior.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h7G=new A.C("typeColumn",B.K,"Column holding the row's type, for excludeTypes + projectType (default type).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h0J=new A.C("excludeTypes",B.a_,'Row `typeColumn` values hidden from every lane (default ["note"]).',B.k,null,!1)
B.he_=new A.C("titleColumn",B.K,"Column shown as each card title.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h_7=new A.C("subtitleColumn",B.K,"Column shown as card subtitle.",B.k,null,!1)
B.haH=new A.C("filterable",B.ab,"Opt-in AddFilterBar over the lanes' full population (before lane splitting) \u2014 same idiom as cards/explorer.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h4E=new A.C("groupByToggle",B.ab,"Show the By-project / Flat toggle (default true).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h2l=new A.C("laneScroll",B.ab,"Each lane owns its own bounded scroll view (default true). Set false when embedding priolanes inside another scrollable (e.g. a scroll:true detail pane) so the inner lane scroll doesn't capture the ancestor's wheel/drag \u2014 the host must then give this node an UNBOUNDED height.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h6o=new A.C("defaultGroupBy",B.T,'"project" or "flat" \u2014 initial group-by (default project).',B.k,null,!1)
B.fVv=new A.C("groupByActions",B.a_,'mokugaps-1019: per-option action for the By-project / Flat toggle \u2014 `{"project": {fn, args}, "flat": {fn, args}}`, fired when the person picks that option (like a segment\'s `action`). A `goto` navigates away and keeps this grouping. Absent = the plain local switch.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h5n=new A.C("edgesTable",B.b1,"Relations table used to walk a task up to its owning project.",B.k,null,!1)
B.aVC=new A.C("edgeFrom",B.K,"Edge column holding the parent id (default from).",B.k,null,!1)
B.aVN=new A.C("edgeTo",B.K,"Edge column holding the child id (default to).",B.k,null,!1)
B.aWf=new A.C("edgeType",B.K,"Edge column holding the relation type (default type).",B.k,null,!1)
B.heE=new A.C("containsType",B.T,"Edge type value meaning containment (default contains).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h2q=new A.C("projectType",B.T,"typeColumn value marking a project/owner ancestor (default group).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h69=new A.C("recencyColumns",B.a_,'Ordered timestamp columns checked to find the Now lane\'s "in motion" row per project group (default [postedAt, editedAt]).',B.k,null,!1)
B.h8D=new A.C("orderColumn",B.K,"Numeric tiebreak column for the in-motion pick (default order).",B.k,null,!1)
B.het=new A.C("action",B.a_,"Card-tap action spec { fn, args }.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h0K=new A.C("pinnable",B.ab,"Show a pinned strip reading the same LocalPrefs pins:<table> key explorer uses, exempt from live filters (default true).",B.k,null,!1)
B.fUn=new A.C("scopeRowId",B.T,'priorun-0801 C1: restrict the lane population to CONTAINS-descendants of this row id (literal id or a $-token resolved via resolveFilterToken, e.g. $rowId / $selected:<table>). FAIL-CLOSED: configured-but-unresolved (token has nothing to resolve to yet, e.g. nothing currently selected) scopes to the EMPTY set, never falls back to the unscoped board \u2014 the anti-leak guarantee a per-project lens depends on. Unset (default) = today\'s unscoped behavior. Shows a "Scoped to: X \u2715" chip when resolved; the \u2715 clears the underlying $selected:<table> selection for token scopes.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h2Q=new A.C("scopeOptional",B.ab,'priorun-0802: opt-in relaxation of scopeRowId\'s fail-closed default \u2014 DEFAULT FALSE, existing behavior byte-identical (still scopes to empty when configured-but-unresolved; a lens must never leak the whole board just because its scope token has not resolved). Set true ONLY for a user-driven SELECTION-CHIP use (e.g. a global view scoped to "whichever row is currently selected", where unresolved means "nothing selected yet", not "the guard rail leaked"): when true and the token is unresolved, renders the FULL unscoped board with no chip; once the token resolves, behavior is identical to the default \u2014 scoped population + the "Scoped to: X \u2715" chip.',B.k,null,!1)
B.haB=new A.C("subtitleMaxLines",B.aM,"dispfb-1018: clamp each card's subtitle (body text) to N lines with an ellipsis (e.g. 3). Absent = unclamped (unchanged). The full text is one tap away (the card opens its item).",B.k,null,!1)
B.hij=new A.C("editAction",B.a_,'dispfb-1018: an explicit EDIT affordance (an "Edit" entry in the card menu) \u2014 `{fn, args}` fired with the card\'s row when the card\'s menu "Edit" entry is chosen. With it set, `action` stays the card-body TAP (e.g. selectRow, navigating the detail panel) and editing is only ever the menu entry. Absent = no Edit entry (unchanged).',B.k,null,!1)
B.hax=new A.C("limit",B.aM,"dispusab-0804: opt-in TOP-N cap PER LANE \u2014 after scope, filters, sort and lane assignment, each lane renders at most N cards. The PREVIEW idiom: a compact lanes strip on an overview screen beside a button that opens the full Priorities view. Per-lane rather than global, because a global cap would silently empty the later lanes. Unset / <= 0 renders every card (byte-identical to before).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h9W=new A.C("colorColumn",B.K,"Optional per-card colour column (a value the engine resolves as a ramp name or #hex).",B.k,null,!1)
B.heh=new A.C("emojiColumn",B.K,"Optional column holding a leading emoji shown on each card.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fV6=new A.C("rankColumn",B.K,'Column holding the manual within-lane sort rank (default "prioRank"); drag-reorder writes it.',B.k,null,!1)
B.dcS=s([B.fUY,B.fTV,B.hbp,B.h4L,B.h7G,B.h0J,B.he_,B.h_7,B.haH,B.h4E,B.h2l,B.h6o,B.fVv,B.h5n,B.aVC,B.aVN,B.aWf,B.heE,B.h2q,B.h69,B.h8D,B.het,B.h0K,B.fUn,B.h2Q,B.haB,B.hij,B.hax,B.h9W,B.heh,B.fV6],t.G)
B.fvz=new A.dv("priolanes",'A three-lane prioritization view over a table\'s status column: Now (active), Pending (queued), Future (discussed). `done` rows and `excludeTypes` rows are hidden \u2014 a forward-looking view, not a full log. Optional project grouping walks CONTAINS edges (same generic edgesTable/edgeFrom/edgeTo/edgeType/containsType idiom as `explorer`/`entrythread`) up to the nearest ancestor whose type equals `projectType`. Drag a card between lanes (wide) or use its \u22ee "Move to\u2026" menu (any width) to rewrite its status through the normal write path.',B.dcS,!1)
B.h4C=new A.C("table",B.b1,"Table the nodes live in (default entries).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h80=new A.C("scopeColumn",B.K,"Opt-in ENGINE scope filter (see `BoardState.rowsForScoped`), only applied to `roots:true` whole-graph mode: root rows are drawn only from `table` rows in the board's currently active scope for (table, scopeColumn) \u2014 the same convention `bubl`/`canvas` read via `activeScope`, so an Outline scoped to the same column as a sibling `bubl`/`canvas` on the same table agrees with them on which rows are in play. Absent (default): unchanged \u2014 every row in `table` mixes at the top level regardless of any ancestor scope.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fXc=new A.C("edgesTable",B.b1,"Relations/edges table to resolve children from.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hc8=new A.C("containsType",B.T,"Edge type value that means containment (default contains).",B.k,null,!1)
B.fUS=new A.C("titleColumn",B.K,"Node column shown as each card title.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h6_=new A.C("subtitleColumn",B.K,"Node column shown as the card body/comment.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fXd=new A.C("orderColumn",B.K,"Numeric column the children sort by.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hcS=new A.C("action",B.a_,"Tap action spec { fn, args } \u2014 fired with the child rowId.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h1z=new A.C("previewInline",B.ab,"Opt-in: show an inline attachment PREVIEW in each card \u2014 image children as a thumbnail, previewable children with an Expand control. Off = the plain title+comment+chip card.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fYi=new A.C("previewColumn",B.K,"Attachments/image column read for the inline thumbnail (default attachment).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h3X=new A.C("previewTypes",B.a_,"List of `type` values that get an Expand-to-embedded-tool control (default wireframe/sheets/docs/sketchpad).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h4I=new A.C("appletColumn",B.K,"Row column giving the applet id for the expanded tool embed (default type).",B.k,null,!1)
B.fTR=new A.C("peekHeight",B.aM,"Height of an inline image thumbnail band (default 160).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h92=new A.C("expandHeight",B.aM,"Height of the expanded (filled-pane) preview; default ~72% of screen height. Expand/Minimize is IN-PANE so the master-detail list stays.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h6L=new A.C("editable",B.ab,"Edit each card's title + comment INLINE (auto-saving notepads), no popup; adds a \u22ee menu (open details / remove from thread).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h__=new A.C("allowAdd",B.ab,'Show an "add an entry" compose bar at the foot of the thread \u2014 creates a note child + a contains-edge so it nests here immediately.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h2e=new A.C("shareAware",B.ab,"Opt-out (default true): when the host has wired an AccessResolver (project sharing), the add-entry/attach compose bar honors canComment(rowId) \u2014 hidden when the current user cannot comment here. Set false to exempt this thread even when the host's hooks are wired globally. Inert when the host wires no hooks.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fUK=new A.C("addHint",B.T,'Placeholder for the add-entry compose bar (default "Add an entry\u2026"); may be a {lang: text} map.',B.k,null,!0)
B.h1q=new A.C("emptyText",B.T,"Empty-state line when the node has no children; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.k,null,!0)
B.h_j=new A.C("removeLabel",B.T,'Card \u22ee menu label for unlinking an entry (default "Remove from thread"); may be a {lang: text} map. Only offered while the entry has another live home \u2014 its only home offers Delete instead.',B.k,null,!0)
B.fYX=new A.C("deleteHistory",B.ab,'logdelete-1008: opt-in no-data-loss mode for the \u22ee Delete text / Delete item options. Each delete first snapshots the entry (or the whole deleted subtree) into a "revision_of" record in edgesTable (empty from, to = the entry; never a containment edge, so it renders nowhere), and the UI offers Restore (stub button / toast). Default false: deletes are undoable only via board undo.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h3n=new A.C("deletedColumn",B.K,'Column stamped (ISO time) by Delete text to mark an entry as a deleted STUB \u2014 content cleared, row + replies kept, rendered as a muted "Entry deleted" line. Default "deletedAt".',B.k,null,!1)
B.h3Z=new A.C("authorColumn",B.K,'Ref column holding WHO added the entry; new entries are stamped with the current user and each card shows a "by <name>" line.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hbR=new A.C("authorTable",B.b1,"Table the author ref points at (default users).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h90=new A.C("authorNameColumn",B.K,"Column giving the author's display name (default name).",B.k,null,!1)
B.hcL=new A.C("authorPicker",B.ab,'Opt-in: the composer shows an "as <name> \u25be" chip to attribute the next entry to any authorTable row (the user\u2194collaborator turn). The choice is sticky and always resolves to a real row.',B.k,null,!1)
B.fTY=new A.C("defaultAuthor",B.T,'Row id (or a value token \u2014 `$setting:<key>` etc., resolved via the shared resolveValueToken) used as the author when the signed-in user is not itself an authorTable row (else the first authorFilter-matching row). Keeps the "by <name>" line from ever rendering blank.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h3r=new A.C("authorFilter",B.a_,'Static { column, value|in } narrowing which authorTable rows can be attributed: the "as \u25be" picker only offers matching rows, and the first-row fallback only draws from them. When configured with NO matching rows, attribution resolves to EMPTY (renders the unattributed state) rather than any arbitrary row. Omitted (default): every authorTable row is eligible, exact prior behavior.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hfK=new A.C("promptingColumn",B.K,"Ref column that records WHO a composed entry is directed at (the turn-taking recipient); written as a one-element list.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hbK=new A.C("promptingPicker",B.ab,'Opt-in: the composer shows a "to: <name> \u25be" chip to address the next entry to a recipient from authorTable ("Anyone" = no target).',B.k,null,!1)
B.hgT=new A.C("awaitingColumn",B.K,"Boolean column set true when a composed entry is directed at someone \u2014 opens the turn so the recipient sees it as pending until answered.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hgs=new A.C("editedByColumn",B.K,"Opt-in: editing a comment/title INLINE stamps this ref column with the current user (+ editedAtColumn=today) \u2014 the inline counterpart of the record editor's edit stamping.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fZB=new A.C("editedAtColumn",B.K,"Opt-in: date column stamped today on an inline edit (pairs with editedByColumn).",B.k,null,!1)
B.hhY=new A.C("parentEditedAtColumn",B.K,'Opt-in: posting a new entry (Add entry / attach / reply) stamps this date column on the THREAD\'S OWN node (nodeId, a row of `table`) with now \u2014 activity counts as an edit, so a task with fresh discussion but no direct field edit still surfaces in "edited recently" filters/sort. No-op unless declared (backward compatible).',B.k,null,!1)
B.h4v=new A.C("attachInline",B.ab,"Show + add attachments right on each card (thumbnails for images, chips for files, an Attach button in editable mode).",B.k,null,!1)
B.fY_=new A.C("attachColumn",B.K,"Attachments column for the inline strip (default = previewColumn).",B.k,null,!1)
B.fUi=new A.C("titleless",B.ab,"Entries are COMMENTS: no title field \u2014 the comment is the card's primary text, the author/time line heads it, and the composer writes the comment column. The composer gains a paperclip for attachment-only entries (when attachInline).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h7o=new A.C("timeColumn",B.K,'ISO-8601 text column stamped on new entries and shown as a relative "\xb7 2h ago" beside the author.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hiC=new A.C("createTypes",B.a_,'Tool types creatable from the log (e.g. ["wireframe","sketchpad"]): the composer gains a "+ tool" menu (new typed entry) and a plain note\'s \u22ee menu gains "Add <tool> here" (sets its type once).',B.k,null,!1)
B.fXJ=new A.C("surface",B.ab,"Wrap the log in a tinted rounded AREA (cards go white with borders) so it reads as its own region apart from the detail header.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hcg=new A.C("caption",B.T,"Small caption line rendered inside the log area, above the entries.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fTA=new A.C("roots",B.ab,"Whole-graph mode: the top level is EVERY idea that nothing flows into (each chain root plus every loose / disconnected idea) instead of one anchored thread, so no `id` is needed. Pair with `nested` to expand each root into its full sub-chain \u2014 a readable outline of the entire graph.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hcJ=new A.C("nested",B.ab,"Every entry is a thread of its own: its contains-children render as nested sub-entry cards (recursive, cycle-safe) and each card gains a Reply affordance. In this mode a card's \"Attach\u2026\" menu creates a CHILD of the picked tool type (the entry stays a comment) instead of converting the entry's own type.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hdA=new A.C("parentColumn",B.K,"Physical containment column on the ROWS table: a row whose parent column points at another renders as its CHILD (and never as a root), alongside edge children \u2014 so an idea nested inside a bubble reads as nested in the outline. Absent \u2192 edges only.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h91=new A.C("anyEdgeType",B.ab,"Treat EVERY edge as a containment edge, ignoring edgeType/containsType. For graphs whose edges are all one relation, and for data whose edges were saved without a type (older data / links drawn on a canvas) \u2014 otherwise the type filter rejects them and the tree renders flat. Default off (type-filtered); new edges are still stamped with containsType.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hbt=new A.C("rootFilter",B.a_,'ideasgraft-1026, `roots` mode: which rows may LEAD the outline, in the shared `filter` grammar (e.g. {"column":"inbox","empty":true} keeps unfiled captures out of the top level). Only the root candidates are filtered \u2014 a filtered row still nests under its parents. Absent = every root, unchanged.',B.k,null,!1)
B.dfT=s(["section","only"],t.s)
B.hgd=new A.C("ownAttachments",B.T,'Opt-in (dufb-1017): "section" pulls the node\'s OWN attachmentTypes children (files on the task/project itself) out of the comment stream into a labelled section above it; "only" renders just that section (e.g. a project overview files block). Comment attachments stay inside their comments.',B.dfT,null,!1)
B.hee=new A.C("ownAttachmentsLabel",B.T,'Header for the ownAttachments section (default "Attached here").',B.k,null,!0)
B.h1d=new A.C("ownAttachmentsEmpty",B.T,'Empty line for ownAttachments "only" mode.',B.k,null,!0)
B.h0O=new A.C("attachmentTypes",B.a_,'Child `type` values treated as attachment OBJECTS (e.g. ["image","wireframe","sheets","docs","sketchpad"]). At the LOG level each renders as a proper ENTRY CARD housing its object (author line + tile/inline editor) in stream order \u2014 never a loose tile on the log surface; INSIDE a comment they render as tiles on that entry. Tap opens FULL-SCREEN (back returns to the log).',B.k,null,!1)
B.h_G=new A.C("excludeTypes",B.a_,"Child `type` values the thread never shows (they belong to another surface \u2014 e.g. sub-tasks listed in a rail tree).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h49=new A.C("collapseToggle",B.ab,"Show a log-header toggle that collapses/expands EVERYTHING at once: comments clamp to one line, attachment previews fold to chips. Per-attachment minimize/show picks reset when toggled.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fVE=new A.C("attachmentsStartMinimized",B.ab,"Inline-editable attachment previews start as compact CHIPS; tap a chip (or its menu) to open the live preview.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h04=new A.C("composeCard",B.ab,'Compose AS a card: "Add entry" (and Reply, in nested mode) creates the entry immediately and opens it as an editable card \u2014 title (optional) + comment + Attach \u2014 instead of a one-line composer bar.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hcc=new A.C("addEntryLabel",B.T,'Label for the compose-card add button (default "Add entry").',B.k,null,!1)
B.h8Q=new A.C("searchable",B.ab,"Show a search box above the log that filters entries by comment text + author name. A match keeps its ancestors so nested replies are not orphaned; empty query shows everything.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fVk=new A.C("searchHint",B.T,'Placeholder for the search box (default "Search\u2026").',B.k,null,!1)
B.haG=new A.C("searchSource",B.T,'Where the query comes from: "app" reads the GLOBAL app-header search (board.searchQuery) and hides the in-body box, so one header search filters the log. Omit for the node\'s own in-body search box.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h2X=new A.C("attachInlineEdit",B.ab,"Render attachment tiles whose type is in inlineEditTypes as a LIVE, bounded, EDITABLE embed (not just a tap-only tile), with an Expand-to-fullscreen control. Other attachment types stay tap-to-open tiles.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h1P=new A.C("inlineEditTypes",B.a_,'Attachment `type` values that get the inline editable embed when attachInlineEdit is on (default ["wireframe","docs"] \u2014 the types with a solo screen).',B.k,null,!1)
B.h4c=new A.C("typeIcons",B.a_,"devflow-1012: per-attachment-kind tile icon, `{kind: iconName}` (names: smartphone, phone_iphone, devices, web_asset, dashboard, image, table_chart, description, brush, attachment). Wins over the built-in icon for that kind; unknown names/kinds fall back to the built-in or generic attachment glyph.",B.k,null,!1)
B.heu=new A.C("typeLabels",B.a_,'devflow-1012: per-attachment-kind display name, `{kind: label}`, used on tiles and in the "New <label>" menus. Wins over the built-in friendly name; absent = built-in name, else the raw kind.',B.k,null,!1)
B.fTU=new A.C("logEntryColumn",B.K,"projdash-0810 fix-forward: opt-in boolean column stamped `true` on every entry this node CREATES (the compose/reply path) \u2014 marks it as log chatter rather than a first-class project item, so a host explorer node's matching `overviewLogColumn` can exclude it from the per-project Overview dashboard's counts. Pair the two props with the SAME column name. Unset (default) is a no-op: entries are written exactly as before this prop existed.",B.k,null,!1)
B.cPe=s([B.h4C,B.h80,B.fXc,B.aVC,B.aVN,B.aWf,B.hc8,B.fUS,B.h6_,B.fXd,B.hcS,B.h1z,B.fYi,B.h3X,B.h4I,B.fTR,B.h92,B.h6L,B.h__,B.h2e,B.fUK,B.h1q,B.h_j,B.fYX,B.h3n,B.h3Z,B.hbR,B.h90,B.hcL,B.fTY,B.h3r,B.hfK,B.hbK,B.hgT,B.hgs,B.fZB,B.hhY,B.h4v,B.fY_,B.fUi,B.h7o,B.hiC,B.fXJ,B.hcg,B.fTA,B.hcJ,B.hdA,B.h91,B.hbt,B.hgd,B.hee,B.h1d,B.h0O,B.h_G,B.h49,B.fVE,B.h04,B.hcc,B.h8Q,B.fVk,B.haG,B.h2X,B.h1P,B.h4c,B.heu,B.fTU],t.G)
B.fv5=new A.dv("entrythread","A thread-forward view of one node's CONTAINS-children (resolved via an edges table): each child renders as a readable card (title + comment + type chip), tap to open. Pair with a bindRow detail so `rowId` is the selected node.",B.cPe,!1)
B.fYv=new A.C("excludeArchived",B.ab,'dufb17a-0924: drop rows hidden by the ARCHIVE lifecycle (rows whose incoming edges are all type "archived", plus their contains-subtrees), read via the scope* edge keys. Scoped views already never reach them; this covers whole-table use. Absent/false = unchanged.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h_u=new A.C("title",B.K,"Column shown as each card title.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fTI=new A.C("subtitle",B.K,'Column shown as a muted subtitle. Also honored by `density:"row"` (wikipick-acceptfix-0831): set, the row tile grows from one line (44-52px) to two (58-68px) to fit it, ellipsized to one line; absent (default), the row stays exactly the single-line tile it always was.',B.k,null,!1)
B.fVq=new A.C("groupBy",B.K,"Group cards into sections by column.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fZW=new A.C("groupFilter",B.a_,'Restrict group HEADERS when grouping by a reference column: { column, value } \u2014 only referenced rows whose column==value become group sections (e.g. group tasks only by project-kind units: {"column":"kind","value":"project"}).',B.k,null,!1)
B.h01=new A.C("valueLabels",B.a_,"Opt-in raw-value \u2192 display map for rendered DATA VALUES (group section headers, tag pills, subtitle, expandFields values): {raw: text-or-{lang:text}} or column-keyed {column: {raw: ...}}, resolved against the ambient locale; unmapped values render exactly as before (passthrough, never blank). Display-only \u2014 stored values, groupOrder matching and tag `colors` keys stay RAW.",B.k,null,!1)
B.a18=s(["board"],t.s)
B.fUm=new A.C("configSource",B.bU,"Subscribe to the BOARD shared data config: \"board\" applies the dataset's shared filters/sort (data_config.dart) before this node's own grouping/search/filter/sort refinements \u2014 the same opt-in used by `map`/`report`, so a cards view can share filters with a sibling view of the same table (e.g. a map\u21c4cards toggle).",B.a18,null,!1)
B.hbA=new A.C("filterableColumns",B.mD,"Curated allowlist of columns offered in the Filter & sort panel (filter fields, sort dropdown, group-by dropdown). Unset = every schema column (except id), unchanged. Set this to hide implementation-detail columns (raw lat/lon, derived sort keys) from the user-facing filter UI.",B.k,null,!1)
B.dgd=s(["spine","flow"],t.s)
B.h3N=new A.C("layout",B.bU,'archhome-0912: opt-in NARRATIVE layout for a view whose order is the point, so a designed structure need not degrade into a generic card list. "spine" draws a vertical time spine \u2014 a hairline rail down the left with one dot per card, and the `spineLabel` value printed ONCE in mono above each consecutive run of cards sharing it (day-group headers). "flow" stacks the cards as stages with a short connector line BETWEEN consecutive cards, read per-row from `connectorColumn` (or the static `connector` string); the connector describes what happens after THIS card, so the last card never draws one. Both force one column at every width and own their own vertical spacing. Presentation only \u2014 same tiles, taps and data; unset (default) or an unrecognised value renders exactly the classic grid.',B.dgd,null,!1)
B.hfN=new A.C("spineLabel",B.K,'With `layout: "spine"`: the column whose value is the mono day-group marker above each run of cards sharing it (e.g. a "2026-09-12" or "Today" stamp). Unset draws the rail and dots with no markers.',B.k,null,!1)
B.fWm=new A.C("connectorColumn",B.K,'With `layout: "flow"`: the column holding the connector text drawn BELOW each card (what happens next, e.g. "lands after tests pass"). Empty on a row draws plain spacing, never an empty band.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h8Y=new A.C("connector",B.T,'With `layout: "flow"`: a static connector string used when `connectorColumn` is unset or empty for a row (e.g. "\u2193").',B.k,null,!1)
B.fU8=new A.C("monoColumns",B.mD,"Columns whose rendered value is a STAMP (a build id, a version, a time code), not prose: those values render with a monospace fallback family and tabular figures so a column of them lines up. Applies to the card/row subtitle today. Unset (default) changes nothing.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h5d=new A.C("phoneColumns",B.aM,'Number of columns to keep at PHONE width (default 1, clamped 1-3) \u2014 the only opt-out from the one-column-on-phone rule, for a genuinely matrix-shaped view where one column per cell would lose the comparison (e.g. a dev|prod pair per component, grouped by component). Ignored by `layout: "spine"`/`"flow"`, which are single-column by definition, and no effect above phone width.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h_c=new A.C("masonry",B.ab,"Lay cards out as a staggered masonry wall (variable-height tiles in independent columns) instead of the uniform grid. Off by default.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hfH=new A.C("minCardWidth",B.aM,"Target minimum card width in px driving the column count (default 280, clamped 160-640); the grid packs more cards as the board widens rather than stretching a few very wide. Phones stay one column regardless.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h5O=new A.C("search",B.ab,"Show a search box at the top.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h5K=new A.C("typeToSearch",B.ab,"Desktop/web: start typing on the idle view to begin a search without clicking the box first (needs search:true). Inert on touch.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hbU=new A.C("searchColumns",B.mD,"Columns the search matches.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hdU=new A.C("searchSource",B.T,'Set "app" to read the GLOBAL app-header search (board.searchQuery) instead of an in-body box, so the header search filters these cards. The in-body search field is then hidden.',B.k,null,!1)
B.fUZ=new A.C("sortBy",B.K,"Column to sort cards by.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fY4=new A.C("sort",B.a_,"Static sort applied before grouping { column, dir: asc|desc } \u2014 an alternative to sortBy/sortDir when the sort must run pre-grouping.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h8A=new A.C("starColumn",B.K,"Generic star: each card's title gets a trailing tap-to-toggle star icon bound to this boolean column; starred cards sort ahead of unstarred ones within whatever sort/grouping is already in effect.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hdS=new A.C("filter",B.a_,'Static pre-filter { column, value|in }. `value` and each `in` element resolve live tokens ($rowId/$playerId/$selected:<table>/$setting:<key>/today/now/uuid) at evaluation time \u2014 e.g. {column: "board", value: "$setting:tasklyCurrentBoard"}. An unresolved token fails OPEN (behaves as unfiltered), not closed \u2014 the opposite of scopeRowId\'s empty-set contract. MAY ALSO be a LIST of such maps, ANDed \u2014 e.g. [{column: "kind", in: ["task","event"]}, {column: "board", value: "$setting:tasklyCurrentBoard"}] \u2014 for a view that needs two constraints at once (each element gets the full per-constraint treatment above, narrowing progressively). Empty list = no constraint.',B.k,null,!1)
B.fZt=new A.C("groupByOptions",B.a_,"Offer a group-by picker: List of { label, column }; the user chooses which grouping is live (overrides the static groupBy).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h3c=new A.C("tableView",B.ab,'The "view as table" toolbar affordance (exportable table sheet) is on by default for every cards node; set false to opt out.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h6s=new A.C("toolbarActions",B.a_,'Extra icon buttons rendered INSIDE the same top search/filter/view-as-table toolbar row \u2014 List of { icon, tooltip, action, position? }, each firing its `action` (same dispatch as any other button) with no row context. Lets an applet add e.g. a "+" new-row button to the toolbar instead of a separate button row above the cards. Each item defaults to LEADING (before the search box \u2014 "[+] [search] [filter] [view]"); set `"position": "trailing"` to place it at the very right instead, after filter/view \u2014 "[search] [filter] [view] [+]". Default empty: no change to any existing applet.',B.k,null,!1)
B.fY0=new A.C("recent",B.aM,'With `collapsible`: show only the first N cards of a section behind a "show all" toggle.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h45=new A.C("open",B.a_,'Label (or {lang: text} map) for an explicit "open" button on each card; absent shows no such button.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h6N=new A.C("pulse",B.a_,'Breathing highlight for "under work" rows { column, value|values }.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h7J=new A.C("tags",B.a_,'Colored pill specs (List of { column, colors }). A NUMERIC column may instead use { column, positiveColor, negativeColor, prefix, suffix } to render a +/- threshold pill (e.g. "+5" green, "-3.4%" red).',B.k,null,!1)
B.h3P=new A.C("imageColumn",B.K,"Column holding a base64 data-uri or image url \u2014 shown as a ~48px rounded leading thumbnail on each card.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hgW=new A.C("badge",B.a_,"Opt-in person badge (ndtags-1109): { typeColumn, value, nameColumn?, colorColumn? } \u2014 a row whose typeColumn equals value leads with a round initials badge (first letters of up to two words of nameColumn/title, coloured by colorColumn). Local labels only.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hcE=new A.C("iconColumn",B.K,"Column holding an icon name or a leading emoji \u2014 shown as a leading accent chip on each card.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fXC=new A.C("accentColumn",B.K,"Column whose value maps (via accentColors) to a colored left stripe.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hhM=new A.C("accentColors",B.a_,"Map of accentColumn value \u2192 ramp name (teal/coral/...) or #hex for the left stripe.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fYd=new A.C("splitBar",B.a_,'wikipick-picture-b2-0831: a slim (4px) two-segment bar rendered under the subtitle on THIS row \u2014 {partColumn, totalColumn, color?, label?}. Reads `partColumn`/`totalColumn` off the row as numbers; the filled segment (partColumn/totalColumn, `color` ramp, default "blue") represents the part, the remainder is a muted outline tint. An optional `label` ({lang: text} map, e.g. "shared") renders after a trailing "part/total" digit pair, same dense-stat convention as the rest of the engine (numbers from data, words from a static localized map \u2014 never mix untranslated words into stored data). Zero/absent totalColumn draws nothing (no divide-by-zero sliver). Fills the one visual gap cards had for a per-row progress/proportion bar (a rollup `progress` node is table-wide, not per-row) \u2014 e.g. a per-seed crawl-progress bar or a per-seed shared-vs-exclusive article split.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hiH=new A.C("emptyIcon",B.T,"Icon name shown on the empty-state panel when the table has no rows.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h0u=new A.C("emptyTitle",B.T,"Headline shown on the empty-state panel when the table has no rows; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.k,null,!0)
B.haZ=new A.C("emptyText",B.T,"Supporting line shown on the empty-state panel; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.k,null,!0)
B.haU=new A.C("emptyAction",B.a_,"Optional empty-state button action spec { fn, args, label }. cards' own convention carries the label inline on this map; the shared `emptyActionLabel`/`emptyActionIcon` props (used by list/tree/agenda) are also honored here and WIN when set, so either authoring style works and both may be set without conflict.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h6A=new A.C("emptyActionLabel",B.T,"Shared empty-state action-button label (same prop list/tree/agenda use). Overrides emptyAction.label when both are set. May be a {lang: text} map.",B.k,null,!0)
B.fW_=new A.C("emptyActionIcon",B.T,"Shared empty-state action-button icon name (same prop list/tree/agenda use). Shown on the button leading edge when set.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fWU=new A.C("collapsible",B.ab,"Collapse long sections behind a toggle.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h86=new A.C("groupsCollapsed",B.ab,"Grouped sections start CLOSED (header only) until tapped open. Calm default for dense registries and nested module lists.",B.k,null,!1)
B.dda=s(["open","expand"],t.s)
B.h4X=new A.C("tapBehavior",B.bU,"tapopen-0830 (BINDING fleet UX standard) + house rule 7a: tapping a card ALWAYS OPENS it \u2014 a generic detail surface with the card's full content \u2014 the configured `action`/`onTap` if set, else the engine's own detail surface. tapfull-0831: on phone that surface is a PUSHED full-screen route (app bar + back), never a slide-up bottom sheet; on desktop/wide it is a full-view centered dialog (house rule 7a \u2014 the old right side-sheet is retired). Set \"expand\" (LEGACY value, kept for source compat) to also guarantee the inline expand-in-place chevron is shown (see `expandChevron`) without needing to opt into it separately \u2014 the body tap itself still OPENS either way; expand-in-place is reachable ONLY via the chevron icon, never the body (house rule 7a: one tap, one outcome).",B.dda,null,!1)
B.h32=new A.C("expandable",B.ab,"Whether this card can expand inline at all (default true). Set false for a card with nothing to expand \u2014 no chevron renders.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h37=new A.C("expandSingle",B.ab,'LEGACY (`tapBehavior: "expand"` only): opening a card collapses its siblings \u2014 at most one card expanded at a time (a card mid-edit keeps its editor).',B.k,null,!1)
B.hcK=new A.C("expandChevron",B.ab,'Shows the expand affordance as an explicit trailing chevron icon (44px hit box) under the default `tapBehavior: "open"` \u2014 the body tap opens the item; only the chevron toggles the inline `expandFields` preview. Under `tapBehavior: "expand"` the chevron is ALWAYS shown (this prop is a no-op there, since expand-in-place has no other affordance once the body tap opens) \u2014 house rule 7a: the card body tap always opens, expand is reachable only via an explicit icon.',B.k,null,!1)
B.a5B=new A.C("height",B.aM,"Optional fixed height.",B.k,null,!1)
B.ddd=s(["outlined","elevated","flat","feature"],t.s)
B.h9k=new A.C("variant",B.bU,"Card treatment (defaults to the style): outlined, elevated, flat, feature.",B.ddd,null,!1)
B.h_B=new A.C("action",B.a_,"Open-record action spec { fn, args }.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h31=new A.C("cardActions",B.a_,"ALWAYS-VISIBLE per-row icon button(s) in the card's title row \u2014 no swipe, no long-press, no expand needed (unlike `swipeActions`, reveal-on-gesture only, or `openActions`, expanded-card only). List of { icon, label, action, column?, equals?, notEquals? }: with `column` set, the button is gated against THIS row's own value (shown only when it equals/notEquals the given value); omitted `column` = always shown. `label` may be a {lang: text} map and is used as the button's tooltip. Each fires its `action` spec on the row through the normal dispatch (chains included). Use for a discoverable \"add without opening\" affordance on a live list, e.g. a search-results card whose row tap reads the item but whose `cardActions` entry saves it \u2014 gated `notEquals` the row's own \"already saved\" flag so a saved row shows its state instead.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hgD=new A.C("longPressActions",B.a_,"Press-and-hold action menu \u2014 same entry shape/gating as `cardActions` (List of { icon, label, action, column?, equals?, notEquals? }). When present (non-empty), it REPLACES the engine's built-in Open/Edit/Delete long-press menu for this node; absent, long-press keeps showing that built-in menu. Either way the popup opens as an anchored contextual dropdown AT the touch point (longpress-anchored-0831), never a slide-up sheet.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hgO=new A.C("rowMenuExtras",B.a_,"Same gated entry shape as `cardActions`/`longPressActions` (List of { icon, label, action, column?, equals?, notEquals?, destructive? }), but APPENDS to the engine's built-in Open/Edit/Delete long-press menu (between Open and Edit) instead of replacing it \u2014 use this when a node wants ONE more contextual action alongside the built-in menu rather than a full custom replacement (rowmenu-extras-0903). An entry with `destructive: true` (e.g. a replacement Delete) renders in the theme's error color, same as the built-in Delete, and is moved to the END of the menu regardless of its position in this list \u2014 non-destructive extras stay between Open and Edit in author order, destructive ones sort after the built-in Delete (rowmenu-extras-destructive-0912).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h8O=new A.C("builtinDelete",B.ab,"Set false to suppress the engine's own row Delete everywhere it would otherwise appear \u2014 the \u22ee overflow menu, the long-press row menu, AND the default \"delete\" swipe entry, all three at once (default true, exact prior behavior when omitted). Use when the applet declares its OWN guarded delete (e.g. confirms an item count, refuses when shared) so a more-discoverable built-in Delete can't bypass it and orphan data.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h1i=new A.C("titleFromColumn",B.K,'Opt-in first-line titles (notes): the card title follows the first line of THIS column (the body) while the stored title column is empty or is itself a first-line derivation; the subtitle then skips that line. An explicit stored title is shown as-is. Display only \u2014 nothing is written. Empty notes show a localized "New note".',B.k,null,!1)
B.fZ1=new A.C("titleAutoColumn",B.K,'Memo column for titleFromColumn (default "titleAuto"); keep it equal to the notepad\'s titleAutoColumn.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hc9=new A.C("expandFields",B.a_,'Extra "label: value" rows shown when a card is expanded. List of { column, label?, format?: currency|percent|compact|relative|number|duration|epochSeconds|epochMillis, decimals?, prefix?, inputUnit?, style? } \u2014 `format` renders the value as a number, or (`relative`) humanizes an ISO-8601 timestamp column as "3m ago"/"2h ago"/"3d ago"; `duration` shows seconds (or `inputUnit:"millis"`) as a compact localized "3d 4h 12m" / "4h 12m" / "12m 5s" (negative \u2192 "\u2014"); `epochSeconds`/`epochMillis` show a Unix timestamp as localized device-time-zone text, `style` = date | time | dateTime (default) | relative. Non-numeric values pass through untouched.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hhK=new A.C("expandDetail",B.a_,"A child node rendered INLINE when a card is expanded, with the row's id injected (and the cards `table` unless the node sets its own). Lets a row edit in place \u2014 e.g. a notepad or embed \u2014 with no popup.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h_U=new A.C("expandHeight",B.aM,"Fixed height for `expandDetail` (default 340). Set it for an embed that needs a bounded canvas.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fVB=new A.C("contentSurface",B.ab,"Render expandDetail on a clean opaque surface so the card tint can't dim an embedded widget/note (default true; set false to opt out).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h6e=new A.C("expandFit",B.ab,"Size `expandDetail` to its content instead of the 340 default \u2014 a short note stays short (the child must self-size, e.g. an autoHeight notepad or an embed with its own height).",B.k,null,!1)
B.fU3=new A.C("editToolbar",B.ab,"An expanded card opens with a compact control row \u2014 an optional `toolbarLead` node, an edit pencil (\u2713 to finish, \u2717 to cancel-and-revert) and a \u22ee options menu \u2014 and `expandDetail` opens read-only until the pencil turns edit on (the `editing` flag flows in).",B.k,null,!1)
B.fTB=new A.C("toolbarLead",B.a_,"A node rendered at the LEFT of the edit toolbar, row-bound (e.g. a `pick` content-type dropdown).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h7x=new A.C("menuActions",B.a_,'Extra \u22ee menu items [{ label, icon?, action }] fired with the row injected (e.g. "Add subtask"); a built-in Delete is always present.',B.k,null,!1)
B.fU4=new A.C("expandExtra",B.a_,"A SECOND inline node below `expandDetail` when expanded, row-bound and content-fit (e.g. a nested cards filtered to this row's children \u2014 a subtask sub-thread, or a box's packed items). Filter it with value \"$rowId\" (the parent's internal id) or \"$parentField:<column>\" (the parent row's value for <column> \u2014 e.g. a plain-number parent key like a box's `number`, when the child table isn't a `ref`). Both tokens also resolve inside `toolbarActions[].action.args.values` (and anywhere else in this spec), so an inline \"+ add\" button can pre-fill the new child row's parent-key field.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h7w=new A.C("expandPeek",B.a_,"A HOST-COMPUTED detail line shown on the EXPANDED card face: { call, tapCall? } \u2014 `call` names a host query ([HostQuery], NOT a synced column) invoked with the row when the card expands; its returned text renders in muted secondary styling below the other expanded content, hidden while pending and hidden entirely when the result is null/empty. Optional `tapCall` names a second host query fired with the row when the line itself is tapped (e.g. open a detail page) \u2014 omit it for a non-tappable line. For read-only, per-viewer, or otherwise host-owned lookup data that must never be written into the board's synced tables (a dictionary lookup, a live status ping, \u2026); the engine never caches the result beyond the card staying expanded. Malformed/absent config renders nothing, byte-identical to before this prop existed.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hgi=new A.C("hideWhenEmpty",B.ab,"Render nothing (no empty notice) when there are no cards \u2014 for a nested sub-thread that should stay invisible until it has rows.",B.k,null,!1)
B.heO=new A.C("autoEditNew",B.ab,"Auto-open a freshly-added row expanded + in edit mode when a host flags it via board.settings[_autoEditRow] (e.g. add-to-thread drops a new empty card already editing). Gated to the row author.",B.k,null,!1)
B.haW=new A.C("addCard",B.a_,'A tappable "add" card ({ label, icon?, action }) AFTER the last item, firing its action with no row \u2014 an inline add affordance that scrolls with the list. With an addCard the empty state is just the add card.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h6t=new A.C("openIcon",B.T,"Under `editToolbar`, the row `open`/action surfaces as this top-right toolbar icon (default open_in_full) instead of a bottom button; the `open` label becomes its tooltip.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h4b=new A.C("openActions",B.a_,'Extra buttons beside the `open` button on an expanded card, each { label, icon?, action } fired with the row injected (e.g. "Show on map" \u2192 focusRow chained with goto). Ignored under `editToolbar`.',B.k,null,!1)
B.d2n=s(["card","row"],t.s)
B.h0k=new A.C("density",B.bU,'Card treatment density. "card" (default) is the classic multi-line card; "row" renders a compact single-line tile (~44-52px): leading checkbox/dot/icon, title, up to 2 trailing tag chips, whole-row tap.',B.d2n,null,!1)
B.fYW=new A.C("sectionLabel",B.T,"An eyebrow header owned by this node, rendered ABOVE its cards \u2014 but ONLY while the list actually has rows right now (reactive: reads the same live row set the node already recomputes). Lets a category caption disappear along with its list instead of sitting over an empty panel (design-real-estate-efficiency \u2014 wikipick-0830ui); may be a {lang: text} map.",B.k,null,!0)
B.hgz=new A.C("combineEmptyAlsoEmptyTable",B.b1,"Opt-in gate so two sibling `cards` nodes on one screen can share ONE combined empty panel instead of each showing its own: this node's authored empty* props render ONLY when this table is empty AND the named sibling table is ALSO currently empty; when the sibling still has rows, this node renders nothing at all (design-real-estate-efficiency \u2014 wikipick-0830ui).",B.k,null,!1)
B.hit=new A.C("dotColumn",B.K,"Column whose value maps (via `colors`) to a small leading color dot \u2014 works in both `density` modes. Falls back to `imageColumn`/`iconColumn` when those are also set (dot is the lowest-priority leading affordance).",B.k,null,!1)
B.hgG=new A.C("toggle",B.ab,"Row density only: show a tappable checkbox as the leading affordance instead of the image/icon/dot, wired to `statusColumn`/`doneValue`/`openValue` (same toggleField convention agenda/tree/list use).",B.k,null,!1)
B.hbL=new A.C("statusColumn",B.K,'With `toggle`: the column read/written by the leading checkbox (default "status").',B.k,null,!1)
B.h3H=new A.C("doneValue",B.T,'With `toggle`: the stored value meaning "done"/checked (default "done").',B.k,null,!1)
B.hdv=new A.C("openValue",B.T,'With `toggle`: the stored value meaning "open"/unchecked (default "todo").',B.k,null,!1)
B.hc_=new A.C("scopeRowId",B.T,"OPT-IN subtree scope (rehome-0804, mirrors `priolanes`' `scopeRowId`): a literal row id or a `$`-token (`$rowId`, `$selected:<table>`). Unconfigured (absent) leaves the card population byte-identical. Configured but UNRESOLVED (e.g. a `$selected:` token with nothing selected) fails CLOSED to the empty set \u2014 never falls back to the whole board. Configured + resolved keeps only rows reachable walking `scopeEdgesTable` DOWNWARD (contains edges) from the resolved row id; the root row itself is included.",B.k,null,!1)
B.AZ=new A.C("scopeEdgesTable",B.b1,'With `scopeRowId`: the edges table to walk (default "relations").',B.k,null,!1)
B.h8C=new A.C("scopeEdgeFrom",B.K,'With `scopeRowId`: the edge\'s parent-id column (default "from" \u2014 matches `priolanes`\' own default; set explicitly when the edges table uses different column names, e.g. "fromId").',B.k,null,!1)
B.AX=new A.C("scopeEdgeTo",B.K,'With `scopeRowId`: the edge\'s child-id column (default "to").',B.k,null,!1)
B.AW=new A.C("scopeEdgeType",B.K,'With `scopeRowId`: the edge-kind column checked against `scopeContainsType` (default "type").',B.k,null,!1)
B.AY=new A.C("scopeContainsType",B.T,'With `scopeRowId`: the edge-kind value meaning "contains" (default "contains").',B.k,null,!1)
B.hfb=new A.C("scopeDepth",B.aM,'With `scopeRowId` (dispfb-1018): `1` narrows the scope to the root\'s DIRECT children only, root excluded \u2014 a one-level "contents of this folder" list. Absent = the default whole-subtree, root-inclusive scope (byte-identical to before).',B.k,null,!1)
B.heo=new A.C("limit",B.aM,'dispusab-0804: opt-in TOP-N cap \u2014 render at most N cards, applied AFTER scope, filter, live search/column filters and sort, so `limit: 3` means "the top 3 of what this view would have shown". The PREVIEW idiom: a compact strip on an overview screen beside a button that opens the full view. Unset / <= 0 renders every row (byte-identical to before); a limit larger than the row count is a no-op.',B.k,null,!1)
B.hbu=new A.C("tag",B.a_,"A SINGLE tag chip spec { column, colors?, positiveColor?, negativeColor?, prefix?, suffix? } \u2014 the singular form of `tags`, appended to whatever `tags` already declares.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h4_=new A.C("colorColumn",B.K,"Column whose value tints the card body, resolved through `colors`. Orthogonal to `accentColumn` (the left stripe) \u2014 a card may carry both.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fYJ=new A.C("colors",B.a_,"Map of value -> ramp name or #hex, shared by `colorColumn` (body tint) and `dotColumn` (status dot).",B.k,null,!1)
