B.h0D=new A.C("action",B.a_,'Row action fired when a step is tapped, e.g. `{"fn":"editRow"}` to open the step\'s detail via the adaptive presentation (right panel on desktop, full-screen page on phone \u2014 never a bottom sheet). Like `canvas`, unset means tap is a no-op (author opts in explicitly).',B.k,null,!1)
B.hbT=new A.C("dataTable",B.b1,"Data overlay: a second table rendered as DATA nodes into the same staged flow. Absent = no data overlay (zero change).",B.k,null,!1)
B.h_x=new A.C("dataStageColumn",B.K,"Data overlay: which stage a data row attaches to. Dragging a data node between stages writes this column only \u2014 never x/y, never an edge row.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hfw=new A.C("dataIntentColumn",B.K,"Data overlay: column rendered as a small badge on the data node \u2014 why it's there (e.g. source / input / derived / output).",B.k,null,!1)
B.fWt=new A.C("dataLinkColumn",B.K,"Data overlay: id of the step row a data row feeds. When set, a light PAINTED-ONLY line is drawn to that step \u2014 no `edgesTable` row is written, so a deleted step just makes the line vanish.",B.k,null,!1)
B.hek=new A.C("filter",B.a_,'Opt-in row scope for `nodesTable` (and, unless `dataFilter` overrides it, `dataTable` too) \u2014 same shape as `bubl`\'s filter: {column, value} or {column, in:[...]}; `value`/each `in` entry may be a token ($selected:<table>, $rowId, $playerId). Absent = all rows (unchanged behavior); resolved value/set EMPTY = no rows, never all. A step/data row freshly created while a resolved scalar {column, value} filter is scoping the view is stamped with that column:value so it stays in scope (e.g. a model-scoped flow: `{"column":"model_id","value":"$selected:models"}`).',B.k,null,!1)
