B.hiB=new A.C("metaPlacement",B.bU,'Opt-in (njnest-1111): "below" \u2014 the expand arrow leads the row and the chips / time / count wrap on a line under the title (roomy on a phone). Default: at the row\'s end.',B.d62,null,!1)
B.h4q=new A.C("example",B.a_,"Opt-in (njnest-1111) example marking, same shape as cards' `example` ({ ids | column, chipLabel?, hiddenFromSetting? }): marked rows carry the chip and drop out while hiddenFromSetting is on.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h6x=new A.C("timeColumn",B.K,"Optional HH:mm column shown on the row.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h6a=new A.C("addedColumn",B.K,'Column for the last-added sort (default "createdAt").',B.k,null,!1)
B.hc2=new A.C("tags",B.a_,'Optional { column, table, labelColumn?, maxShown?, badge? }: tags shown on the row and offered in the filter. badge (ndtags-1109): { typeColumn, value, colorColumn? (default color) } \u2014 a tag whose typeColumn equals value (e.g. group == person) shows as a round initials badge instead of a chip; njnest-1111: { all: true } \u2014 every row of the table is a person. njnest-1111: may be a LIST of such sources (the first drives the filter); a source with no table shows the column\'s own value as a chip, through valueLabels? {value: label} and colors? {value: "#RRGGBB"} (e.g. a mood).',B.k,null,!1)
B.h7t=new A.C("missed",B.a_,"Optional { dateColumn, settingKey, filter }: rows matching filter, dated before today and not done, join the list while the day in settingKey is today, with a Move to today button.",B.k,null,!1)
B.h6h=new A.C("carry",B.a_,'Opt-in carry-through (carry-1108): { startColumn?, doneColumn?, doneAtColumn?, skipIf?: [columns], filter?, label? } or true. An undone row with a start date shows on every day from it on; once done, from start to the doneAt day (no doneAt: the start day only). A set skipIf column (e.g. a time, a repeat) or a row outside filter keeps its own day. The shown day is the filter clause on startColumn; carried rows get a "since Fri \xb7 day 3" line and no Move to today.',B.k,null,!1)
B.h_L=new A.C("settingKey",B.T,'Prefix of the device settings holding sort and filter (default "grouplist").',B.k,null,!1)
B.h5y=new A.C("action",B.a_,"Title-tap action { fn, args } (args get table + id).",B.k,null,!1)
B.he9=new A.C("emptyText",B.T,"One quiet line when there are no rows; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.k,null,!0)
B.hdw=new A.C("fill",B.ab,"Under a root `footer` layout: take the height left in the column and scroll inside it.",B.k,null,!1)
B.ha9=new A.C("newGroupRow",B.ab,'Default true: a "+ New group" line ends the list. false when the app puts it elsewhere (a `groupadd` in a footer\'s `above`).',B.k,null,!1)
B.fZf=new A.C("wideColumns",B.aM,"2 shows groups as cards side by side at 900px and wider; 3 flows them into three columns at 1320px and wider (two from 900px). Default: one list at every width.",B.k,null,!1)
B.heF=new A.C("timer",B.a_,"Opt-in (timers-1108) per-row countdown: { lengthColumn?, endsAtColumn?, leftColumn?, alarm?, presets? } (defaults timerSeconds, timerEndsAt, timerLeft). A row with a length shows m:ss and play; running shows the live time with pause, stop and reset; time's up shows a Stop pill. endsAt is UTC ISO-8601. After each write `alarm` fires with args { op: schedule|cancel, id, title, at }, and once { op: ring, id, title } when a countdown seen running crosses zero. ndfix-1110: savedColumn? (default timerSaved \u2014 \"save for later\" time left, used only when the table has it); restoreAlarms? (true: re-arm running countdowns' alarms once per session, for a cold start); faceColumn? (default timerFace: countdown | countup \u2014 one timer, two faces), elapsedColumn? (default timerElapsed: a stopwatch's banked seconds), track? (true: the time a countdown runs, overtime included, is logged through `tracking`).",B.k,null,!1)
B.hhg=new A.C("tracking",B.a_,"Opt-in (timers-1108) per-row time tracking: { startedColumn?, totalColumn?, log?: { table, refColumn, startColumn, endColumn, secondsColumn } } (defaults trackStartedAt, trackedSeconds, time_logs(page, start, end, seconds)). Shows the total and a clock button; while running a red dot, the live stretch and pause, which logs the stretch and adds it to the total. An active countdown takes the row's slot first.",B.k,null,!1)
B.fXb=new A.C("subtasks",B.a_,'Opt-in subtasks (ndnotes-1109): true or { parentColumn? (default parentId), titleColumn?, doneColumn?, orderColumn?, values?: {\u2026written on each new subtask}, promoteValues?: {\u2026written when reparent makes one top-level}, parentFilter? }. A subtask is a row of the same table whose parentColumn names a live row passing parentFilter, or a subtask itself (ndfix-1110: nesting is unlimited; done/total counts direct subtasks).  Subtasks are not listed as their own rows (nor carry); a parent shows done/total. njnest-1111: doneColumn: false (or the node\'s doneColumn: false) \u2014 no ticks, "N inside", plain "- " bullets in Copy as text; titleFromColumn? (default the node\'s).',B.k,null,!1)
